-- Solar hot water at the Central Heating Plant

How it works: sun-warmed fluid preheats the condensate water the plant turns back into steam. Water that starts warmer needs less fuel to boil, so the plant burns less natural gas for the same steam.

Location: no coordinates of its own; it inherits them from the plant.', NULL, NULL, '5eed0081-d403-5613-ac5d-cdc267d69bfc', false)
